{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1407","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Chocolate Bunny"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We hid from you a permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of the elements from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. You want to guess it. To do that, you can give us 2 different indices $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$, and we will reply with $$$p_{i} \\bmod p_{j}$$$ (remainder of division $$$p_{i}$$$ by $$$p_{j}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We have enough patience to answer at most $$$2 \\cdot n$$$ queries, so you should fit in this constraint. Can you do it?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As a reminder, a permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$2$$$ appears twice in the array) and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$ but there is $$$4$$$ in the array)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of the input contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^4$$$) — length of the permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The interaction starts with reading $$$n$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then you are allowed to make at most $$$2 \\cdot n$$$ queries in the following way: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? x y"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" ($$$1 \\le x, y \\le n, x \\ne y$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After each one, you should read an integer $$$k$$$, that equals $$$p_x \\bmod p_y$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When you have guessed the permutation, print a single line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"! "}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes), followed by array $$$p$$$ and quit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query do not forget to output end of line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python;"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see documentation for other languages."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Exit immediately after receiving \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and you will see "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wrong answer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" verdict. Otherwise you can get an arbitrary verdict because your solution will continue to read from a closed stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hack format"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line output $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^4$$$). In the second line print the permutation of $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n\n1\n\n2\n\n1\n\n0"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n? 1 2\n\n? 3 2\n\n? 1 3\n\n? 2 1\n\n! 1 3 2"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1407C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1407/problem/C"}